        "orario": "11:13",
        "timestamp": 1777194785,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Trumpâs Golden Dome missile shield faces budget squeeze despite Pentagon push TOI World Desk / TIMESOFINDIA.COM / Apr 26, 2026, 14:43 IST Comments AA Small Medium Large Representative AI image President Donald Trumpâs ambitious Golden Dome homeland missile defense initiative is facing growing doubts over funding, congressional support and technical feasibility, even as top Pentagon officials insist the project is moving ahead, according to a report by Politico. Senior Pentagon officials gathered Thursday at Fort Story, Virginia, to showcase progress on the program, which aims to build a nationwide shield against threats ranging from intercontinental ballistic missiles to drones. But behind the public optimism, the project faces steep financial and political obstacles. Trump Goes All-In With BIGGEST-EVER War Budget, Fast-Tracks âGolden Domeâ; Panic Over Iran? The Golden Dome system is expected to cost anywhere between $185 billion and $3 trillion, while the Pentagon is seeking $17 billion through budget reconciliation next year and only $400 million through the normal appropriations process, Politico reported. That strategy is already drawing resistance from Republicans in Congress, who appear reluctant to rely on reconciliation ahead of crucial midterm elections. House Appropriations defense subcommittee chair Ken Calvert told Politico, âIs [reconciliation] the most efficient, effective way to spend money? In my mind, no.â The Golden Dome concept is designed to protect the United States from multiple threats using a network of existing and next-generation systems linked by artificial intelligence capable of sharing battlefield data in real time. Key components are expected to be operational by 2028 to meet Trumpâs timeline. Leading the effort for the Pentagon, Gen. Mike Guetlein defended the programâs viability. âTo the skeptics, let me say this,â Guetlein said. âGolden Dome is achievable. It is not a single point failure.â He added the project is intended to âstrengthen global stability by creating profound doubt in the adversaryâs mind. They will not win.â However, Guetlein acknowledged that many technologies involved remain classified and declined to provide a detailed spending breakdown. âI cannot tell you exactly where the moneyâs going,â he said, adding that the system would combine land, air and space-based assets. âWeâre actually buying hardware. We are not doing prototypes.â Politico reported that one early component is already undergoing domestic testing. The Armyâs Long-Range Persistent Surveillance system, installed at Fort Story, uses a 360-degree sensor array to detect cruise missiles, drones and aircraft. Lawmakers, however, have voiced frustration over the lack of detailed consultation from the administration. Representative George Whitesides said communication had not yet âreached the level of detailed spending plans.â âIâm okay with not pouring a ton of money out the door without having a pretty cohesive view of what it should do,â he said. Questions have also emerged over affordability. Guetlein recently warned lawmakers that space-based interceptors, considered a centerpiece of the shield, may be dropped if costs become excessive. âWe are so focused on affordability.â Guetlein told the House Armed Services strategic forces subcommittee. âIf we cannot do it affordably, we will not go into production.â Golden Dome received around $23 billion last year through a summer reconciliation package, but Politico said those funds were delayed, frustrating defense contractors seeking contracts. Jeff Hanke, president of space systems at L3Harris Technologies, said industry had hoped the process would move faster. âWe just have to continue to work with them, share with them, help them go as fast as they can go.â The White House plans to shift Golden Dome into the base federal budget after 2027 through a dedicated âGolden Dome for America Fund,â with projected allocations rising to $14.7 billion in 2028, $15 billion in 2029, $16 billion in 2030, and $15.8 billion in 2031, Politico reported. For now, the future of Trumpâs signature defense project depends heavily on a Republican-controlled Congress that remains cautious about another reconciliation battle. Acting Pentagon comptroller Jules Hurst said alternative options are already being considered. âWeâll go back to the White House and weâll work with Congress to come up with a new strategy if the White House and Congress decide reconciliation is not the right [path],â Hurst said. End of Article Tired of too many ads? go ad free now Arsenal Missiles Tanks Guns Submarines RS-28 Sarmat Satan II Missiles RS-28 Sarmat Satan II Russia Trident II D5 USA LGM-30G Minuteman III USA RS-24 Yars Russia M51.3 France Agni-V India Hwasong-17 N. Korea RT-2PM2 Topol-M Russia Julang-2 China Agni-V India Agni-P India K-4 India BrahMos India Pralay India Nirbhay India Akash-NG India Astra Mk2 India Rudram-1 India MR-SAM India Iron Dome Tamir Israel David's Sling Stunner Israel Arrow 2 Israel Arrow 3 Israel Jericho III Israel LORA Israel Delilah Israel Popeye Turbo ALCM Israel Spike NLOS Israel Python 5 Israel Derby Israel Patriot PAC-3 MSE USA THAAD USA SM-3 Block IIA USA SM-6 USA Tomahawk Block V USA JASSM-ER USA AIM-120D AMRAAM USA BGM-109 Tomahawk Block IV USA Shahab-3 Iran Emad Iran Sejjil-2 Iran Kheibar Shekan Iran Fattah-1 Iran Soumar Iran Paveh Iran Noor Iran Khalij Fars Iran Shahed-136 Iran Bavar-373 Iran Fateh-110 Iran Russia Missile RS-28 Sarmat Satan II Service Start 2023 Service End Present Range 18000 km Compare Across Missiles Defence Videos 08:03 Iran Expands War Threat: Bab Al Mandeb, Aramco, Yanbu, Fujairah Now In Direct Conflict Line 10:57 Iran Rejects Talks After US Fires On Sanctioned Cargo Ship Touska, Says âBlockade Main Obstacleâ 08:01 NATO IS DEAD? Europe KICKS U.S. Out of 'NEW SECRET BLOC' Amid Trump's Exit Threat Over Iran War 10:05 Nearly 400 U.S. Soldiers Injured In Iran War, Reveals CENTCOM; America Hiding Losses? Defence News Defence | 37 minutes ago Trumpâs Golden Dome missile shield faces budget squeeze despite Pentagon push Defence | 15 hours ago DRDO unveils its Advanced Armoured Platforms, the organisation's pitch for the BMP replacement Defence | 15 hours ago Unmatched & professional: Why nations send their troops to India for training Defence | a day ago USS Rafael Peralta intercepts Iranian vessel before Pakistan talks: All about Americaâs most advanced guided-missile destroyer"
